statement:
Let $(\Omega', \mu)$ be a probability space, let $t \ge 1$, and let $Y_0, \dots, Y_{t-1} : \Omega' \to \bbr$ be mutually independent, almost everywhere measurable random variables that almost surely take values in $[0,1]$. Suppose $\E[Y_i] \le \varepsilon$ for every $i$, where $0 \le \varepsilon$, and let $c > 1$. Then
\[
  \mu\!\left\{\omega \;\middle|\; c\,\varepsilon\,t \le \sum_{i=0}^{t-1} Y_i(\omega)\right\}
  \;\le\;
  \exp\!\left(-2(c-1)^2\varepsilon^2 t\right).
\]
